1. Objective

    Integrate GitHub with Odoo 19 Employee Analytics to collect repository commit activity, associate commits with employees, and display employee-wise contribution details.

2. Work Implemented

    GitHub API integration: Configured GitHub connectivity in Odoo using the required authentication and organization/repository settings.

     Webhook integration: Configured the GitHub webhook endpoint to receive push events and process newly pushed commits in Odoo.

     Commit synchronization: Implemented synchronization for configured repositories and branches, including retrieval of commits from the configured 2026 start date.

     Employee mapping: Connected GitHub commit author information with the corresponding Odoo employee using the configured GitHub username/email mapping.

     Duplicate handling: Used commit-level identification to avoid creating duplicate commit records when synchronization is repeated.

     Employee Analytics dashboard: Added employee-wise GitHub commit counts to the Employee Analytics Dashboard and enabled navigation from an employee's commit card to the related commit records.

     Date filters: Added commit statistics for day, week, month, quarter, year, all-time, and custom date ranges.

     Manual synchronization: Used the GitHub synchronization action in Odoo to retrieve repository and commit data, including historical backfill.

3. Synchronization and Testing Activities

    Tested the GitHub integration in the QA environment.

    Verified repository and commit synchronization through the Odoo GitHub Integration settings.

    Ran synchronization for configured repositories and reviewed the synchronization summary.

    Checked employee-wise commit counts and dashboard navigation.

    Reviewed GitHub API rate-limit behaviour after synchronization requests were restricted.

4. Outcome

    GitHub commit integration and the Employee Analytics dashboard functionality have been implemented. The synchronization workflow has been exercised and its results reviewed. The recorded API rate-limit restriction is a validation constraint for completing any remaining repository/commit backfill.

5. Key Features Available

    GitHub push-event capture through the webhook.

    Repository and branch-based commit synchronization.

    Employee-wise commit statistics.

    Date-range filtering for commit counts.

    Commit details accessible from the Employee Analytics Dashboard.

    Manual synchronization for historical commit retrieval.